  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q20-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The line $ax+by+1=0$ is perpendicular to $4x+3y=7$ and passes through $(9,7)$. Find the values of $a$ and $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=3$, $b=-4$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3y&=-4x+7\\\\y&=-\\frac43x+\\frac73\\end{align*}$$The perpendicular gradient is $\\frac34$. Using the point $(9,7)$:$$\\begin{align*}y-7&=\\frac34(x-9)\\\\4y-28&=3x-27\\\\3x-4y+1&=0\\end{align*}$$Comparing with $ax+by+1=0$ gives $a=3$ and $b=-4$. Check: $3(9)-4(7)+1=0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
